  /Alt (The map displays a geographic tiling scheme overlaid on a satellite imagery base map of Europe and its adjacent regions, including the North Atlantic, Arctic, North Africa, and the Middle East. Land areas are shown with natural colours (green for vegetation, white for ice, brown for desert), and water bodies are dark blue. A grid of red lines defines individual tiles, each uniquely labelled with light blue alphanumeric codes such as `h15v05`, `h16v02`, `h17v03`, `h18v04`, `h19v04`, `h20v05`, and `h21v04`. A grey outline highlights the extent of land masses within the mapped area. The map includes a north arrow in the top-left corner and a scale bar indicating distances from 0 to 2,000 km in increments of 500 km. The Coordinate Reference System (CRS) is specified as `ETRS89-extended / LAEA Europe (EPSG:3035)`.)
